<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 11.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 11.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Thursday.</p>
<p>P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		   P/E	 Close</p>
<p> 1 Portman Min	     295.24   1.86</p>
<p> 2 Niugini Min	     273.38   3.80</p>
<p> 3 Mayne Nickless	  198.64   8.78</p>
<p> 4 T N T		     172.66   2.40</p>
<p> 5 Colonial Coml	   119.13   2.18</p>
<p> 6 Adel Bton Cement	118.84   1.64</p>
<p> 7 Herald Rsc		 92.92   1.05</p>
<p> 8 Forrestania Gold	 88.89   2.24</p>
<p> 9 Westral Forest	   74.28   2.05</p>
<p>10 Cape Range		 72.97   0.27</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1 Dominion Min		2.77   0.67</p>
<p> 2 Computer Power	    3.42   3.50</p>
<p> 3 Premier Inv		 4.11   0.73</p>
<p> 4 Parbury Ltd		 5.88   0.69</p>
<p> 5 BTR Plc		     5.91   5.50</p>
<p> 6 Aust Gold Rsc	     6.58   1.20</p>
<p> 7 Pac Mutal Aust	    6.75   2.41</p>
<p> 8 McIntosh Sec		6.83   0.85</p>
<p> 9 OLS Asia Hldgs	    7.23   0.86</p>
<p>10 Capcount Prop	     7.87   0.86</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
